\omega_{S,k_{2y}-k_{1y}}&\sim&\omega_{S,k_{2y}-k_{0y}}+\frac{k_{0y}-k_{2y}}{\omega_{S,k_{2y}-k_{0y}}}(k_{1y}-k_{0y}).\nonumber
\eea
Let us define the positions
\beq
x_{\tau}=x_0+\frac{k_{0x}}{\nomvk0}\tau\hsp
y_{\tau}=y_0+\frac{k_{0y}}{\nomvk0}\tau\hsp 
y^S_{\tau}=\frac{k_{2y}-k_{0y}}{\omega_{S,k_{2y}-k_{0y}}}\tau.
\eeq
Then $J$ can be rewritten
\beq
J(\vk_1,\vk_2,k_{2y}-k_{1y},\tau)=e^{-\sigma^2(k_{0x}-k_{1x})^2+ix_{\tau}(k_{0x}-k_{1x})-\sigma^2(k_{0y}-k_{1y})^2+i(y_{\tau}-y^S_\tau)(k_{0y}-k_{1y})-i\tau(\nomvk0+\omega_{S,k_{2y}-k_{0y}}-\nomvk2)}
\eeq
and so the evolved state is
\bea
e^{-iH\p t}|\Phi\rangle_0\bigg|_{O(\sl)}&=&-i\pi\sigma^2\sqrt{\lambda}\npinvk2e^{-it\nomvk2}\int_0^t d\tau e^{-i\tau(\nomvk0+\omega_{S,k_{2y}-k_{0y}}-\nomvk2)}|\vk_2\rangle_0\\
&&\ \ \times
