Simply speaking, an isomorphism $\alpha$ maps nodes and edges of
$G$ to nodes and edges of $H$ in such a way that the image of the edge
connects the image of the source of this
edge to the image of the target, as in Figs. \ref{fig:iso} and 
 \ref{fig:iso-auto}).

