Now we consider the full set of input isomorphisms:

\begin{definition}{\bf Symmetry groupoid.}
The {\em symmetry groupoid}\index{symmetry !groupoid } of the network is defined as the set of
all symmetry isomorphisms of the network~\citep{stewart2006}:
\begin{equation}
\begin{array}{l}
{\rm Symmetry \,\, groupoid}=\\ \{\tau_{i\to j}\ |\ \tau_{i\to
  j}\ {\rm is\ a\ symmetry \ isomorphism \ from}\ i \to j \}\ .
\end{array}
\end{equation}
\end{definition}


