First of all, we computed one additional year and measured the difference \eqref{eqn:StoppingCriterion} afterwards. The results are show in Fig. \ref{fig:results-4a}. To interpret the values therein, we note that the final value of the spin-up norm in the test-data after a spin-up of 10'000 years are in the range of $10^{-5}$ to $10^{-4}$, which is shown in Fig. \ref{fig:results-4b}.
