%\begin{abstract}
%We build a state-of-the-art dynamic model of private asset allocation. Like existing models, we capture the illiquidity and capital commitment lags associated with private equity. Our model further considers important features of PE investing that challenge investors, including (1) business cycle conditions, (2) serial correlation in observed PE returns, and (3) regulation-induced portfolio constraints. We use cutting-edge machine learning methods to quantify the optimal investment policies over the life cycle of a fund. Our model can also be used by regulators to assessed the costs and benefits of different choices of risk-based capital charges.
