\caption{\label{fig:R_vs_eps} Order parameter $R$ as a function of perturbation strength $|\epsilon|$ for (left to right) Erd\H{o}s--R\'enyi (ER), Barab\'asi--Albert (BA), and Watts--Strogatz (WS) networks. Upper panels: enhancement from $R \approx 0.2$ ($K = 0.2$, 0.3, 0.85 for ER, BA, WS respectively); lower panels: suppression from $R \approx 0.8$ ($K = 0.55$, 0.6, 6.0). Filled symbols indicate adversarial attack intervention intervals for a: {\Large $\bullet$} ($\tau = 0.1$), $\blacksquare$ ($\tau = 0.3$), $\blacktriangle$ ($\tau = 0.5$), $\blacktriangledown$ ($\tau = 0.7$), and 
